{
 "_sources": {
  "2x2": "per item, cue-factorial set (e10 <m>_cues.jsonl CoT text + CoT answer); last relational claim by claim_parse v3 over e2f split_sents; agree = answer implied by the written front object equals the CoT answer; denominators = cue items with a parsed last claim; twin-pair (image) cluster bootstrap 2,000. Twins / Syn. Depth 431 versions in 'twins' / 'syn431'.",
  "dvis": "imgswap.json full:all dvis (Tab. supp_recheck 'full R, all'): own full rationale, image v -> identity-swapped twin v_cf, 800 twin queries per model; full:wrongR = items whose rationale has a wrong claim.",
  "edit": "claim_edit_uncond.json 'all' (Tab. supp_claim_uncond): Synthetic Depth (500 images) + occlusion twins ('in front' phrasing), items whose stored rationale has a parsable first claim, all four Direct x CoT cells; edit at the first claim, same-turn continuation.",
  "S_orig": "relation_sensitivity.json: S = P(follows appended gold conclusion) - P(follows appended wrong conclusion) under R_cut, original image, CV-Bench 2D left/right items (Fig. 4 value) and depth items (CV-Bench 3D Depth + Synthetic Depth); checker = rationale-body checker (InternVL3-8B, InternVL3.5-8B, Qwen2.5-VL-7B), copier = the rest.",
  "commit": "commit_baseline.json / commit_nulls.json (Tab. supp_commit_nulls): D+C- rationales of the 2,850-item pool (Sec. 5 cells, e2b trajectories); commit share = rationales with a commit j* / all D+C-; relational share = rule-typed relational j* / committed."
 },
